{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 4, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 3059177738203722275, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 633, "mtime": 1791871702.6179848, "sha256": "62ce14c5369936f5cb839bc9d2bda9bd0bb88619158b3156af8608738b0804f8"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 434, "mtime": 1791871705.7821748, "sha256": "560dc49c6217773dec45cab7fd65f10e8b94a4fb155006e0ac8e2f82c36c5a50"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/1/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/1/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test that covers both failure modes: the binary representation and banker's rounding on exact halves.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so the old `round(x, 2)` rounded it down. `round()` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit, so `round(0.125, 2)` gave `0.12`, which isn't half-up either.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): convert the float to its shortest exact string (`repr(2.675)` \u2192 `\"2.675\"`, the number the customer sees), then round to cents with `Decimal.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)`. It still returns a float, so `add_vat` and other callers don't change.\n\n**Verification:** pytest isn't installed here, so I didn't run the test suite. I ran the cases directly instead; first column is the input, second the old `round()` result, third the new result:\n\n| input | old | new |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2.675 | 2.67 | 2.68 |\n| 0.125 | 0.12 | 0.13 |\n| 1.005 | 1.0 | 1.01 |\n| 2.674 | 2.67 | 2.67 |\n| -2.675 | -2.67 | -2.68 (halves round away from zero) |\n\n`split(10.00, 3)` still gives `[3.34, 3.33, 3.33]`. I added `tests/test_round_money.py` with these cases; the old code fails the first three.\n\n**Remaining risk:** `add_vat` multiplies floats before rounding. If a product lands just off a half-cent (e.g. `\u202649999999`), its shortest string still ends that way and it rounds down. Fixing that properly means doing the VAT calculation in `Decimal` too; I didn't change it because it wasn't part of this request.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 10, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 273864, "requests_cache_write": 18038, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1945508, "requests_count": 10, "requests_input_uncached": 22, "requests_out